## 2026-07-22 — First live paper pilot (OANDA practice + local PaperBroker)

### What shipped
- OANDA v20 adapter scaffold: `live/oanda.py`, specs `OANDA_V20_REFERENCE.md` / `OANDA_ADAPTER.md`, vendored `v20-python/`.
- Mid-signal / bid-ask fill bar schema (`Bar` quote book + `QuoteOneMinuteBarBuilder`); PaperBroker buys at ask / sells at bid when quotes present.
- **Pilot A** parallel demos under `live/demo/` (not `live/state/`):
  - EURUSD → `EUR_USD`
  - NAS100 → `NAS100_USD` (NQ-ish)
  - SPX500 → `SPX500_USD` (**ES proxy**)
  - US30 → `US30_USD` (**YM proxy**)
- Same strategy on all four: `v2b_scaleout` OCO ungated, `S_1_1_1`, `use_regime_filter=false`, NY RTH gate, PaperBroker only (no OANDA order routing).
- CLI: `demo-{eurusd,nas100,spx500,us30}-v2b-paper` (+ `-status` / `-stop`), `--daemon`.

### Bugs found in pilot and fixed
- OR clock: v2b `_parse_dt` now converts to `America/New_York` (UTC `Z` bars were skipping OR).
- Order expiry: `_session_expiry` emits NY-offset 15:59; PaperBroker `_ts_after`/`_ts_before` timezone-aware (naive `T15:59:00` vs UTC caused noon ET cancels).
- Stream resilience: reconnect/backoff after overnight disconnect.

### Pilot posture (explicit)
- This is the **first paper pilot system**: OANDA practice **prices in**, local **PaperBroker** fills out.
- Tradovate futures paper and OANDA **order routing** remain next phases (see `LIVE_FEED_PAPER_TRADING_EXECUTION_PLAN.md` + OANDA burn-in checklist).
- Runtime artifacts under `live/demo/*/state|charts|pidfile|*.log` stay local (gitignored).

### Open follow-ups from pilot day
- Stop **trigger** still uses mid high/low; fill price uses ask/bid — tighten quote-side triggers later.
- Sibling strategies (`or_2r_fade`, `v2b_clean_break`) still have old `_parse_dt` / naive expiry stamps.
- Full OR/OCO on index CFDs starts next RTH (today’s OR window already passed when SPX/US30 came up).
- OANDA practice order burn-in checklist items 6–11 still open before any live routing.

